Subject: [PATCH] benchmarks/verified/golden_geometry/repro_cmd.sh: resolve the repo root one level up

The script sits at <repo>/benchmarks/verified/golden_geometry/repro_cmd.sh, so the repo
root is three levels up from $here, not two.  With ../.. the script resolved $repo to
<repo>/benchmarks and died immediately:

  $ sh benchmarks/verified/golden_geometry/repro_cmd.sh
  python3: can't open file '<repo>/benchmarks/benchmarks/verified/golden_geometry/run_benchmark.py'
  rc=2

Audit m17870 found this by running the command the README/result.json advertise; the
underlying benchmark itself was fine (30 rows / 9 gates PASS when invoked directly).
Verified after the fix: rc=0, 30 rows identical to artifacts/golden_benchmark/result.json.

--- a/benchmarks/verified/golden_geometry/repro_cmd.sh
+++ b/benchmarks/verified/golden_geometry/repro_cmd.sh
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 set -eu
 
 here=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)
-repo=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$here/../.." && pwd)
+repo=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$here/../../.." && pwd)
 out=${1:-"$repo/artifacts/golden_benchmark"}
 
 cd "$repo"
